course: dictionary
lesson: 7062
title: Paternity and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Paternity is a formal word about being a child's father. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «Parents get time off work, called maternity and paternity leave, to look after a new baby.» Maternity is about mothers, so the word next to it, paternity, must be about fathers.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Paternity leave is time off work for a new father.» Swap in "time off work for a new father" and it still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Leave tells you it is time off, and new baby tells you who it is for.
explain: Paternity has a few meanings. In adult life, it means the time off work a dad gets when his baby is born. In law, a paternity test shows who a child's father is. A more formal meaning is where an idea or work came from, or who started it.
fact: Paternity means being a child's father.
fact: «Paternity leave» means time off work that a father gets when his baby is born.
fact: «Maternity» is the matching word for mothers, so it is a useful clue.
fact: In Britain, paternity leave is usually two weeks, as one example sentence says.
fact: A «paternity test» shows who a child's father is.
exercise: «Paternity leave is time off work for a new father.» What does paternity leave mean? | *Time off work for a new father | A holiday for the whole family | A lesson about old fathers | Time off school for a new baby
exercise: «Parents get time off work, called maternity and paternity leave.» Which word is the matching word for mothers, and helps you see that paternity is about fathers? | Parents | Baby | *Maternity | Leave
exercise: Mia reads «The paternity test showed who the child's father was.» What is a paternity test for? | To plan a family picnic | *To find out who a child's father is | To measure how tall a child is | To check a baby's teeth
test: «Paternity pay» is money a father may get while he is on paternity leave. What is paternity pay? | Pay for a new bike | Money a child gets for a birthday | *Money a father may get while on paternity leave | A bill for a family dinner
test: «Nobody knows the paternity of this old story.» In this sentence, what does paternity mean? | The name of the main character | How many pages the story has | Whether the story is funny | *Where the story came from, or who started it
exam: Which sentence uses paternity to mean time off work for a new dad? | A new dad goes back to school | Dads always wear hats to work | Paternity is a kind of rain | *Paternity leave gives a dad time off work to look after his new baby
